__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pem
*.key
*.log
# Rotated logs too -- *.log does NOT match bot.log.1/.2/.3, so 10MB
# rotations kept showing up as untracked and were one `git add -A`
# away from being committed.
*.log.*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Nothing under data/ is tracked, and nothing under it may be re-tracked.
# Five calibration files (city_weights, condition_weights,
# metar_lockout_calibration, seasonal_weights, temperature_scale) used to be
# force-added past this rule so a fresh clone had a starting point. The cost
# was that `git restore .` or `git checkout -- data/` silently reverted
# learned calibration to whatever was last committed -- no warning, no error,
# and nothing downstream noticing. The fresh-clone copies now live in seeds/
# and paths.materialize_missing_seeds() copies them in when, and only when,
# data/ does not already have them. Do NOT `git add -f` anything here again;
# tests/test_paths.py::TestNothingUnderDataIsTracked fails the build if you do.
data/
.claude/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.db
.worktrees/
